          "title": "You'll want to know: cliēns, clientis",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "cliēns, clientis — \"a client, a dependant\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Clientēs māne ad domum patrōnī veniunt. The clients come to their patron's house in the morning."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "cliēns, clientis m. A client owed his patron greeting and support; the patron owed him protection and help at law. English client."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "cliēns is usually traced to an old verb clueō \"to hear, to be called\" (Lewis & Short): one who listens to his patron. English client comes from it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
