            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Nāviculārius frūmentum trāns mare vehit. The shipowner carries grain across the sea."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "nāviculārius, nāviculāriī m., built on a little word for a ship, from nāvis. The great grain ships of Rome were run by nāviculāriī."
            }
          ]
        },
