              "text": "librārius, librāriī — \"a copyist, a scribe; a bookseller\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Librārius librōs dīligenter scrībit. The copyist writes out books carefully."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "librārius, librāriī m., built on liber, a book, with a short i. Copyists were often slaves trained to write a fast clear hand."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "librārius is built on liber, librī \"a book\" (Lewis & Short), with the ending -ārius of a man busy with something. English library comes from the same word through French."
            }
          ]
        },
