              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "agrīmēnsor, agrīmēnsōris — \"a land surveyor\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Agrīmēnsor fīnēs agrī mētītur. The surveyor measures the boundaries of the field."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "agrīmēnsor, agrīmēnsōris m., from agrī, of a field, and mētior, to measure (participle mēnsus). A late word, in Ammianus and Cassiodorus."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "agrīmēnsor is built from agrī, the genitive of ager \"a field\" and mēnsor \"a measurer\" (Lewis & Short), the agent noun of mētior \"to measure\"."
            }
          ]
        },
